Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 382dcb6dc1b1ff5ecf39a980b98b93f6c741ede0&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="503124" author="adilger" created="Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:22:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Some thoughts on how to implement this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;each file should have a common suffix like &lt;tt&gt;.ltsh&lt;/tt&gt; (Lustre Test Shell) so it can ignore helper scripts, editor backup files, etc. and if we start having &lt;tt&gt;.ltpy&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;.ltrs&lt;/tt&gt; subtests they can also be identified&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;useful information should be encoded in a comment at the start of each test fragment:
	&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;minimum number of OSTs, MDTs, etc. needed&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;minimum client or server version to run test (replaces monolithic &lt;tt&gt;lustre/tests/except/$TESTSUITE.ex&lt;/tt&gt; files)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;minimum free filesystem blocks and inodes&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;filesystem should be mounted or unmounted at start of subtest&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;filesystem will be reformatted at start/end of subtest&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;IMHO, it should be possible to have multiple related subtests in a single file, for example because they need a common set of helper functions or test configuration that shouldn&apos;t be recreated by each subtest.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think the best way to start using this is to add the infrastructure to &lt;tt&gt;test-framework.sh&lt;/tt&gt; (or possibly another &lt;tt&gt;test-fragments.sh&lt;/tt&gt; file?) that can load subtests from a &lt;tt&gt;$TESTSUITE.d/&lt;/tt&gt; directory (e.g. &lt;tt&gt;lustre/tests/sanity.d/&lt;/tt&gt;) and then start adding &lt;em&gt;new&lt;/em&gt; subtests there.  We can incrementally move existing subtests to be test fragments, but this would likely need to be done one/few per patch because of the two &lt;tt&gt;review-dne-subtest-change&lt;/tt&gt; sessions running each subtest in a loop for 30m.  If we split all 1100 of the sanity.sh subtests into fragments in a single patch it would launch 2200 sessions and consume 45 days of runtime and probably not be able to pass since some subtests are not robust against running in a loop...&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
